WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.260
A cucumber slice sits overnight in salty water.

2
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.960
It gets lighter and goes soft.

3
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.340
A slice in plain distilled water gets heavier.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Something crossed the edge of the cells, in opposite directions.

5
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.660
How does a cell control what gets in and out?

6
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.920
And why does salt water make lettuce wilt?

7
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:32.463
Every cell has a cell membrane, a thin boundary around the cell.

8
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:38.503
It is a double layer of fatty molecules called phospholipids, with proteins in it.

9
00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:40.723
It is selectively permeable.

10
00:00:41.543 --> 00:00:44.643
Some things cross easily, and others hardly at all.

11
00:00:45.663 --> 00:00:48.223
Small molecules such as oxygen slip through.

12
00:00:49.163 --> 00:00:53.443
Charged ions such as sodium and chloride cross only through proteins.

13
00:00:54.417 --> 00:01:00.237
Passive transport moves a substance from more concentrated to less concentrated.

14
00:01:00.917 --> 00:01:02.637
The cell uses no energy.

15
00:01:03.417 --> 00:01:05.857
That difference is a concentration gradient.

16
00:01:07.137 --> 00:01:11.957
Molecules move at random, so more cross from the crowded side than come back.

17
00:01:12.797 --> 00:01:14.817
Diffusion is this spreading out.

18
00:01:15.797 --> 00:01:19.337
Facilitated diffusion is diffusion through a membrane protein.

19
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:25.750
Osmosis is the net movement of water across a selectively permeable membrane.

20
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:31.630
On balance, water moves toward the side with more dissolved solute, because that

21
00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:33.430
side has less free water.

22
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.350
Saltier outside is hypertonic, and water leaves.

23
00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:41.330
Less salty outside is hypotonic, and water enters.

24
00:01:42.530 --> 00:01:45.510
Equal is isotonic, and water crosses both ways.

25
00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:51.170
Active transport uses energy from the cell, often from ATP.

26
00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:55.430
It can move a substance against its concentration gradient.

27
00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.130
In animal cells, the sodium potassium pump spends ATP.

28
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:05.490
It moves three sodium ions out and two potassium ions in.

29
00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.550
Both trips go uphill.

30
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:10.370
Without ATP, the pump stops.

31
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:13.043
Now back to the cucumber.

32
00:02:13.743 --> 00:02:19.443
The salty water was hypertonic to its cells, so on balance water left them by

33
00:02:19.443 --> 00:02:23.943
osmosis. A plant cell has a stiff wall outside its membrane.

34
00:02:24.783 --> 00:02:27.723
Water flowing in makes the cell press on the wall.

35
00:02:28.363 --> 00:02:30.243
That push is turgor pressure.

36
00:02:31.163 --> 00:02:36.023
In salty water the cells lose water and turgor, so the slice goes soft.

37
00:02:36.943 --> 00:02:38.343
Lettuce wilts the same way.

38
00:02:38.343 --> 00:02:44.023
The membrane chooses what crosses, and water moves toward more solute.
